<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>netstandard2.0;net462;net8.0;net10.0</TargetFrameworks>
	<PackageId>CodexMicroORM.Core</PackageId>
	<Version>1.4.1</Version>
	<Authors>CodeX Enterprises LLC</Authors>
	<Company>CodeX Enterprises LLC</Company>
	<Product>CodexMicroORM.Core</Product>
	<Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026, All Rights Reserved</Copyright>
	<PackageTags>ORM microORM entity-framework database object-mapping micro-ORM entity data-access dataset linq-to-sql</PackageTags>
	<GeneratePackageOnBuild>true</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
	<PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>false</PackageRequireLicenseAcceptance>
	<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/codexguy/CodexMicroORM</PackageProjectUrl>
	<Description>A high performance, low code alternative to ORM's such as Entity Framework, offers intelligent database mapping to your existing CLR objects with minimal effort. Visit "Design Goals" on GitHub to see more rationale and guidance.</Description>
	<PackageReleaseNotes>
1.4.1 - Fixes a permanent ServiceScope leak.

ServiceScope.Dispose advertised disposal as its LAST statement, but that callback is
what pops the scope off the ambient stack and restores the previous current scope. Any
throw before it skipped the pop, so the scope stayed rooted for the life of the async
flow and the current-scope pointer was left referencing a disposed scope. The unwind now
runs in a finally.

The throw that exposed it: disposal asked "is there a connection scope to close?" through
the create-on-read CEF.CurrentConnectionScope, so a scope that never opened a connection
would manufacture one during its own disposal - and that constructor throws when no data
provider is configured. Disposal now peeks instead of creating, matching what the other
branch already did.

Measured on an affected workload: ambient scope depth went from +22.00 per call (dead
linear) to 0.00, managed memory from 350-&gt;645MB and climbing to flat, and calls ran about
20% faster with the spurious connection scopes gone.

No public API change; AssemblyVersion intentionally stays 1.4.0.0 so existing binding is
unaffected. System.Text.Json and System.Collections.Immutable are no longer forced on
net8.0 consumers - they are now referenced only for netstandard2.0 and net462, which is
where they are actually needed.
	</PackageReleaseNotes>
	<!-- Patch release: AssemblyVersion deliberately NOT bumped. Moving it would break
	     assembly binding for anything compiled against 1.4.0.0 (this package still ships a
	     net462 target, where that means a binding redirect). Version/FileVersion carry the
	     release identity; AssemblyVersion follows major only. -->
	<AssemblyVersion>1.4.0.0</AssemblyVersion>
	<FileVersion>1.4.1.0</FileVersion>
	<PackageLicenseExpression>Apache-2.0</PackageLicenseExpression>
	<PackageIcon>xSkrapeIcon.jpg</PackageIcon>
	<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>

	<!-- Source/symbol publishing. SourceLink is in the SDK from .NET 8, so this needs no
	     package reference. Debugging INTO this library from a consuming app is how its last
	     bug was found; a snupkg and a repo URL make that a step instead of an afternoon. -->
	<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/codexguy/CodexMicroORM.git</RepositoryUrl>
	<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
	<PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
	<EmbedUntrackedSources>true</EmbedUntrackedSources>
	<IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
	<SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Deterministic paths only on a build server. Setting this locally rewrites source paths
       in the PDB and makes stepping into a locally-built copy harder, which is the opposite
       of what the symbol settings above are for. -->
  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(CI)' != '' or '$(TF_BUILD)' != '' or '$(GITHUB_ACTIONS)' != ''">
	<ContinuousIntegrationBuild>true</ContinuousIntegrationBuild>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Debug|AnyCPU'">
    <NoWarn>1701;1702;IDE0008;IDE0058;IDE0047;IDE0060;VSSpell001</NoWarn>
  </PropertyGroup>
	<PropertyGroup Condition="'$(Configuration)|$(Platform)'=='Release|AnyCPU'">
		<!-- CS0162 (unreachable code) deliberately NOT suppressed: Release is the configuration
		     that ships, so it is the last place to be hiding it. -->
		<NoWarn>1701;1702;IDE0008;IDE0058;IDE0047;IDE0060;VSSpell001</NoWarn>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="DatabaseProviders\**" />
    <EmbeddedResource Remove="DatabaseProviders\**" />
    <None Remove="DatabaseProviders\**" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Compile Remove="ObjectServices\Infrastructure\ValueTrackingWrapper.cs" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="C5" Version="3.0.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="Newtonsoft.Json" Version="13.0.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Only the frameworks that do NOT ship these in-box. Referencing them unconditionally put
       System.Text.Json 10.x and System.Collections.Immutable 10.x in the net8.0 dependency
       group, i.e. version-10 packages forced onto a version-8 runtime, which is a version
       conflict waiting to happen for any consumer pinning the 8.x line. The net10.0 group
       already resolved to neither, which is what made the asymmetry visible. -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(TargetFramework)' == 'netstandard2.0' or '$(TargetFramework)' == 'net462'">
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.CSharp" Version="4.7.0" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Collections.Immutable" Version="10.0.9" />
    <PackageReference Include="System.Text.Json" Version="10.0.9" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <None Include="xSkrapeIcon.jpg">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
    <None Include="..\README.md">
      <Pack>True</Pack>
      <PackagePath></PackagePath>
    </None>
  </ItemGroup>

  <Target Name="PostBuild" AfterTargets="PostBuildEvent" Condition="$([MSBuild]::IsOSPlatform('Windows')) and Exists('C:\\Source\\WizerFood\\WizerFoodWeb\\SharedBin\\')">
    <Exec Command="xcopy $(TargetDir)*.* C:\Source\WizerFood\WizerFoodWeb\SharedBin\ /y /c" />
  </Target>

</Project>
